Ceph/RADOS support
==================

Build
-----

Needs the librados C client (rados/librados.h and librados), e.g. the librados-dev or
librados-devel package.

    cmake -DENABLE_RADOS=ON <path to eckit>

For an installation in a non standard location:

    cmake -DENABLE_RADOS=ON -DRADOS_ROOT=<prefix of the Ceph client> <path to eckit>

Configuration
-------------

Resource (environment variable)                     Default
radosClusterName ($ECKIT_RADOS_CLUSTER_NAME)        ceph
radosClusterUser ($ECKIT_RADOS_CLUSTER_USER)        none, must be set, e.g. client.<name>
radosClusterConf ($ECKIT_RADOS_CLUSTER_CONF)        ~/.ceph/ceph.conf
radosMaxWriteSize                                   90 MiB  (osd_max_write_size)
radosMaxObjectSize                                  124 MiB (osd_max_object_size)

Tests
-----

The tests carry the "rados" label and need a running cluster:

    ctest -L rados

They work in an existing pool, each in a namespace of its own:

    cmake -DENABLE_RADOS=ON -DECKIT_RADOS_TEST_POOL=<pool> -DECKIT_RADOS_TEST_USER=client.<name> ...

Without these cmake variables the tests read ECKIT_RADOS_TEST_POOL and ECKIT_RADOS_CLUSTER_USER from
the environment. With -DENABLE_RADOS_TESTS_MANAGE_POOLS=ON the tests create and destroy pools named
test_handle, test_kv and test_performance instead, which needs a user allowed to do so and
mon_allow_pool_delete on the cluster.
